                    "label": {
                        "en": "Description"
                    },
                    "value": {
                        "en": "Shows Mahmud ibn Sebuktegin, ruler of the Turkish Ghaznavid Dynasty from 998 to 1030CE, conquering Qasdar in India. The fortress of Qasdar can be seen to the right of the image, with several archers on its battlements, with the troops of Sebuktegin, also armed, to the left of the scene. Arguably the greatest treasure in the library, the Jami' al-Tawarikh, or Compendium of Chronicles, is a world history which encompasses a range of cultures, from China in the East, to Ireland in the West, from the time of Adam. It is written in the Naskh script and contains 70 illustrated folios."
